   "answer": ["A"],
   "flag": "The key rests on a Control Tower preventive control that denies deletion of the company's own audit log buckets, but the control reference shows no managed control that denies deletion of customer-chosen buckets outright: the closest elective preventive control (AWS-GR_RESTRICT_S3_DELETE_WITHOUT_MFA) only denies S3 delete actions without MFA, so a principal with MFA can still delete; the mandatory bucket-deletion controls protect only the buckets Control Tower creates in the log archive account. Option C (a custom SCP attached in Organizations) is then the only option that verifiably blocks every principal, so the stem needs a constraint or option A needs rewording (for example a custom SCP control deployed to the OU).",
